{"title":"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The diagonals have been drawn in the square shown.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The area of the shaded region of the square is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/a/a8a0330f9330fc0fbf271353e79a86029820b4b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 4 \\text{ cm}^{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 8 \\text{ cm}^{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 16 \\text{ cm}^{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 56 \\text{ cm}^{2} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 64 \\text{ cm}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"549\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the side length of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90e5a8a73cda70a0edb9da30d1eb81198dd5c551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, the full area of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f6008fdeab769e92f1f3fb455dd9af0a0b8c37b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^{2} = 64 \\text{ cm}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Each triangle adds up to the area of the square and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of them, so the area of each triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/c/eacd2bf539324895bbd4eed08fdd9946aff47d1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{64}{4} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 16 \\text { cm}^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"147\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The side lengths of a square are equal to each other and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangles can stack to create the height of a triangle, so the base of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90e5a8a73cda70a0edb9da30d1eb81198dd5c551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> and the height of the shaded triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abd8e30048c006566815b2871d9e94366145eafb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{2} = 4 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>The area of the shaded triangle is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f50541929119ce1992a643a36cbc5a1447c2a06e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8 \\times 4}{2} = \\frac{32}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3f3d5f5a079498e1f472525c6db521ef610b02a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 16 \\text { cm}^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" title